// Article 1: three equal stripes, with the width contained twice in the length: 1:2, on
// a grid of 18 by 36. Five stars in the white, four forming an oblong parallel to the
// stripes, the fifth at its center.
// From elsewhere: the oblong spans a third of the length, 12 to 24, and each star's
// circle is 1/18 of the length, radius 1 (FOTW, from the decree's figures). So the outer
// star centers are at 13 and 23. The rows at 7.5 and 10.5 are from the Commons drawing.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Honduras"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "Apache-2.0"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20250505000030id_/https://infosen.senado.gob.mx/sgsp/gaceta/65/2/2022-09-06-1/assets/documentos/Ofic_Secretaria_Relaciones_Exteriores_Cambio_Cromatica_Pabellon_Hondureno.pdf"
  source "https://www.crwflags.com/fotw/flags/hn.html"
  source "https://www.elheraldo.hn/honduras/cambia-color-bandera-honduras-vuelve-azul-marino-congreso-nacional-PI29037459"
  source "https://elheraldo.hn/honduras/diputado-propone-establecer-azul-turqui-color-oficial-bandera-nacional-CD32136127"
  source "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_of_Honduras"
  note "The color here is the law's turquoise blue, not what the state now flies. Since January 2026 the Congress and government have used navy blue again, as they did until 2022, with no change in the law found. A bill to make it azul turquí in law was filed on 23 September 2026, and whether it has passed wasn't confirmed."
  note "Article 1's text was read as Honduras's foreign ministry circulated it in 2022, in a note filed with Mexico's Senate. Its header reads as a reform of Decree No. 7. The press and FOTW identify that reform as Decree No. 29 of 18 January 1949, which wasn't read in La Gaceta."
  note "The star's size and the oblong's width are FOTW's account of figures in the decree, measured by a contributor from a civic booklet of 1965. He gives the star as 1/18 of the \"flag width\", read here as the length, which is what the Commons drawing also has. The star rows are from the Commons drawing."
  note "Pantone 3105 C is the foreign ministry's of 2022. The hex is not a conversion of it: it's the one Wikipedia reports from the National Autonomous University, and the Album des Pavillons 2023 gives the same RGB for Pantone 306 C, as reported by FOTW. White is plain white."
  law "Legislative Decree No. 7 of 16 February 1866, as reformed, Article 1" {
    source "https://web.archive.org/web/20250505000030id_/https://infosen.senado.gob.mx/sgsp/gaceta/65/2/2022-09-06-1/assets/documentos/Ofic_Secretaria_Relaciones_Exteriores_Cambio_Cromatica_Pabellon_Hondureno.pdf"
  }
  law "Legislative Decree No. 29 of 18 January 1949"
}
palette {
  blue "#00bce4" {
    pantone "3105 C"
    reference "Album des Pavillons 2023, as reported by FOTW" "Pantone 306 C, CMYK 71-0-8-0"
  }
  white "#ffffff"
}
proportion hoist=18 fly=36

bars blue white blue
charge star blue {
  radius 1
  at fly=13 hoist=7.5
  at fly=13 hoist=10.5
  at center
  at fly=23 hoist=7.5
  at fly=23 hoist=10.5
}
